From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sangbaek Park <sangbaekpark@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 08:32:34 -0700
Subject: media: Check IsCleared in VideoImageRepresentation read access

VideoImageRepresentation::BeginScopedReadAccess() was missing an
IsCleared() check before granting read access to the underlying
SharedImage backing. When hardware video encoders consume an uncleared
SharedImage created without initial pixel data, uninitialized GPU
memory could potentially be encoded and returned in the bitstream to a
compromised renderer.

This CL adds an unconditional IsCleared() check to
VideoImageRepresentation::BeginScopedReadAccess(), matching sibling read
representations (Skia, Overlay). It also corrects the AccessMode passed
to ScopedAccessBase in VideoImageRepresentation::ScopedReadAccess from
kWrite to kRead.

A new unit test is added to SharedImageRepresentationTest to ensure
uncleared SharedImages cannot be read via VideoImageRepresentation, and
existing tests are updated with SetCleared().

Bug: 553118338
Change-Id: I26a41b6579230d2c2854dcf6eaba25665a3b2e71
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8298633
Reviewed-by: Vasiliy Telezhnikov <vasilyt@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Sangbaek Park <sangbaekpark@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1690766}

